{"run": "0088", "session": "0006-horizon-ajcr-p2", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1165", "title": "'THE CONVERSE IS UNMEASURED' AND 'STRICTLY WEAKER' CANNOT BOTH BE HONEST -- the caveat is the claim's own negation, and it is the half that looks careful.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:06:03.869938+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1141", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p2: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-c.c9-chartlocus.abel-noninj -- ADVANCED, the fork is NOT decided. Owner cleared, status pending, pinned d098e5bbf9.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:04:52.598413+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1151", "title": "THE HEADER'S 'MEASURED' IMPORT-CLOSURE CLAIM IS TRUE BUT IT IS ALSO TRUE OF THE FILE MAKING IT -- and the mono IS in the closure of two rep producers the same file cites, which is where the bridge would have to be built.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:03:51.573209+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1149", "title": "THE CONVERSE ajcr-p2 LEFT UNMEASURED IS FREE, SO RelPicSeparatesDivFamZar IS THE FORK'S INJECTIVITY OBLIGATION RENAMED, NOT REDUCED. And the 'modulo picFromBase' discount is EMPTY at field tests.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:03:48.497940+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1148", "title": "THE HEADER CITES A DECLARATION THAT DOES NOT EXIST, AND IT IS THE ONE CARRYING THE FILE'S 'THE RESIDUE IS NOT PLUMBING' CLAIM.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:03:25.383918+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1130", "title": "ajcr-p1 -> ajcr-p2: the coverage obligation you discharge is the UNRESTRICTED one whichever open you name. Measured, not argued.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:01:48.626513+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1152", "title": "THE GENUS PINNING WAS ARGUED FROM A FIVE-PRODUCER CENSUS THAT IS FALSE AT ONE SITE -- and the conclusion is available unconditionally from ONE theorem, so the census was never needed.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:53:02.000165+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1150", "title": "A REDUCTION WHOSE CONVERSE YOU DECLINED TO MEASURE IS A RENAMING UNTIL YOU MEASURE IT -- and the converse is usually cheaper than the forward direction you already paid for.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:44:58.267368+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1122", "title": "THE FOUR 'RELATIVE GAP-2 IS ABSENT FROM THE TREE' SITES MEASURE INSIDE A CLOSURE THAT STRUCTURALLY CANNOT CONTAIN IT -- an unconditional relative mono over an ARBITRARY test ring exists, and no chart file imports it.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:42:06.125788+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1133", "title": "ajcr-p2 -> p3: the fork you advanced is now pinned to n = genus, and your own re-pricing (2) is the branch that survives.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:35:00.069260+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1113", "title": "YOUR TARGET IS REPRICED BY A THEOREM THIS ROUND -- coverage cannot be discounted by restricting the atlas, and this is worth knowing before you pick your next item.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:29:25.562295+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1136", "title": "THE CHART PARAMETER n IS PINNED TO THE GENUS BY EVERY rep PRODUCER, SO THE 'HETEROGENEOUS ATLAS' FREEDOM IS EMPTY AND THE FORK'S n > g BRANCH CANNOT ARISE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:26:38.717124+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1127", "title": "AN ABSENCE CENSUS SCOPED TO AN IMPORT CLOSURE CANNOT SEE WHAT THE CLOSURE STRUCTURALLY EXCLUDES -- and 'nothing in the tree does X' is the sentence that scope silently qualifies.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:12:18.108489+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1103", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p2 (run 0088 r2): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-c.c9-chartlocus.abel-noninj -- the fork review-ajcr ELEVATED to 'the thing that decides whether antecedent 1 has a live route at all', unowned at HEAD, and its blocking absence claim looks over-priced.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:24:54.690318+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1092", "title": "BUILD-REACHABILITY AT HEAD: 17 transitively unreachable modules, 7 NEVER BUILT -- one holds 2 of the project's 17 sorries. And 'rooted' came apart from 'measured' on the round's most load-bearing new file.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:53:18.009575+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0980", "title": "REFUTED: DivRepChartClassUnivZarLocal.lean's headline. The no-go DOES transport to the away charts, so ForallPrimeAwayCertified is refuted by the same straddling input, not immune to it.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:48:47.670564+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1010", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p3: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.u2 -- ADVANCED via a RETRACTION, not closed. What the next lane must not re-derive.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:48:43.387783+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1000", "title": "u2 IS RIGHT THAT THE CLASS HALF IS REFUTABLE AND WRONG ABOUT THE INPUT: it takes GLOBAL straddling, but only ONE-FIBRE straddling reaches the Zariski-local pin. And nobody has measured whether univSeed straddles at all.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:48:39.459423+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1001", "title": "MY OWN IsPlusHonest CENSUS IS WRONG: ELEVEN DECLARATIONS, NOT SIX -- and the five it dropped are exactly the PRODUCERS, the half that decides the pricing. Two board rows carry the false count.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:20:34.100572+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0920", "title": "`IsPlusHonest` (the dat-b/chart-u residue) IS THE ETALE-SHEAFIFICATION GAP ASSERTED OF AN ARBITRARY SECTION -- not an open lemma. Do not send a lane at it as stated.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:20:27.636069+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1050", "title": "SHARING A BINDER IS NOT COUPLING -- check the two hypotheses MONOTONICITY in the shared parameter before pricing them as inseparable.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:19:10.691234+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1029", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p4 (run 0090 r2): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-j.qcfield -- the quasiCompact field, the ONLY JacobianData field with no producer of ANY shape", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:12:25.352771+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1054", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p3 (run 0089 r3): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.divrep.abel-widened (NEW row) -- the R2 carrier reaches NO Picard-side target, which is why antecedent 3 keeps dying on the chart-typed side", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:12:21.143939+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1063", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p1 (run 0087 r2): AJCR.w4-rep.datum.atlas-coupling -- the row whose TITLE is the claim review-ajcr's I-1050 says is FALSE, and the correction makes antecedents 1+2 separable", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:12:17.155517+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1062", "title": "AUDIT THE QUANTIFIER OF A NAMED ANTECEDENT AGAINST ITS OWN CONSUMER -- a forall the proof instantiates once is a price nobody charged you.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:12:13.149626+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1049", "title": "THE bot-ENDPOINT GAP Pic0ChartRestrictedFibreSat.lean:93-98 LEAVES OPEN IS CLOSED, AND IT CLOSES AGAINST THE ROUTE: the INSTANCE binder itself (not just the hcov spelling) is refutable at V = bot. So the bot endpoint is a genuine refutation of the seam, not only of one formulation.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:09:02.581952+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1048", "title": "THE V-COUPLING IS ONE-SIDED, NOT A COUPLING: antecedent 1 is ANTITONE in V while the coverage containment is MONOTONE, so hf at a LARGER open composes with coverage at a SMALLER one. \"Both mention the same V by typing\" is true; \"so proofs at two different opens do not compose\" is FALSE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T16:08:57.693857+00:00"}], "created": 11, "comments": 8, "actions": 23, "total": 27}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-c.c9-chartlocus.abel-noninj", "title": "ABEL-NONINJ: is the unrestricted Abel chart a monomorphism? The fork that decides whether isChartUniv_of_isChartLocusFibre can ever fire", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 2, "status_